 Python v3\\.14\\)\"), completely decoupled from code specific to **urllib3**\\.\n\nAt the very core, just like its predecessors, urllib3 is built on top of [http\\.client](https://docs.python.org/3/library/http.client.html#module-http.client \"\\(in Python v3\\.14\\)\") – the lowest level HTTP library included in the Python standard library\\.\n\nTo aid the limited functionality of the [http\\.client](https://docs.python.org/3/library/http.client.html#module-http.client \"\\(in Python v3\\.14\\)\") module, urllib3 provides various helper methods which are used with the higher level components but can also be used independently\\.\n\nclass urllib3\\.util\\.Retry\\(*total=10*, *connect=None*, *read=None*, *redirect=None*, *status=None*, *other=None*, *allowed\\_methods=frozenset\\(\\{'DELETE', 'GET', 'HEAD', 'OPTIONS', 'PUT', 'TRACE'\\}\\)*, *status\\_forcelist=None*, *backoff\\_factor=0*, *backoff\\_max=120*, *raise\\_on\\_redirect=True*, *raise\\_on\\_status=True*, *history=None*, *respect\\_retry\\_after\\_header=True*, *remove\\_headers\\_on\\_redirect=frozenset\\(\\{'Authorization', 'Cookie', 'Proxy-Authorization'\\}\\)*, *backoff\\_jitter=0\\.0*, *retry\\_after\\_max=21600*\\)\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\nRetry configuration\\.\n\nEach retry attempt will create a new Retry object with updated values, so they can be safely reused\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n```\nretries = Retry(connect=5, read=2, redirect=5)\nhttp = PoolManager(retries=retries)\nresponse = http.request(\"GET\", \"https://example.com/\")\n\n```\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n```\nresponse = http.request(\"GET\", \"https://example.com/\", retries=Retry(10))\n\n```\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\nErrors will be wrapped in [MaxRetryError](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.exceptions.html#urllib3.exceptions.MaxRetryError \"urllib3\\.exceptions\\.MaxRetryError\") unless retries are disabled, in which case the causing exception will be raised\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  Set to `0` to fail on the first retry\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  How many connection-related errors to retry on\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  Set to `0` to fail on the first retry of this type\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  How many times to retry on read errors\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  Set to `0` to fail on the first retry of this type\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  Set to `0` to fail on the first retry of this type\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  How many times to retry on bad status codes\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  Set to `0` to fail on the first retry of this type\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  How many times to retry on other errors\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  Set to `0` to fail on the first retry of this type\\.\n\n  If `total` is not set, it’s a good idea to set this to 0 to account for unexpected edge cases and avoid infinite retry loops\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  Set of uppercased HTTP method verbs that we should retry on\\.\n\n  By default, we only retry on methods which are considered to be idempotent \\(multiple requests with the same parameters end with the same state\\)\\. See [Retry\\.DEFAULT\\_ALLOWED\\_METHODS](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html#urllib3.util.Retry.DEFAULT_ALLOWED_METHODS \"urllib3\\.util\\.Retry\\.DEFAULT\\_ALLOWED\\_METHODS\")\\.\n\n  Set to a `None` value to retry on any verb\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  A set of integer HTTP status codes that we should force a retry on\\. A retry is initiated if the request method is in `allowed_methods` and the response status code is in `status_forcelist`\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n  seconds\\. For example, if the backoff\\_factor is 0\\.1, then [Retry\\.sleep\\(\\)](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html#urllib3.util.Retry.sleep \"urllib3\\.util\\.Retry\\.sleep\") will sleep for \\[0\\.0s, 0\\.2s, 0\\.4s, 0\\.8s, …\\] between retries\\. No backoff will ever be longer than backoff\\_max\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n- **history** \\([tuple](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#tuple \"\\(in Python v3\\.14\\)\")\\) – The history of the request encountered during each call to [increment\\(\\)](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html#urllib3.util.Retry.increment \"urllib3\\.util\\.Retry\\.increment\")\\. The list is in the order the requests occurred\\. Each list item is of class `RequestHistory`\\.\n\n- **respect\\_retry\\_after\\_header** \\([bool](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#bool \"\\(in Python v3\\.14\\)\")\\) – Whether to respect Retry-After header on status codes defined as [Retry\\.RETRY\\_AFTER\\_STATUS\\_CODES](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html#urllib3.util.Retry.RETRY_AFTER_STATUS_CODES \"urllib3\\.util\\.Retry\\.RETRY\\_AFTER\\_STATUS\\_CODES\") or not\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n- **retry\\_after\\_max** \\([int](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#int \"\\(in Python v3\\.14\\)\")\\) – Number of seconds to allow as the maximum for Retry-After headers\\. Defaults to [Retry\\.DEFAULT\\_RETRY\\_AFTER\\_MAX](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html#urllib3.util.Retry.DEFAULT_RETRY_AFTER_MAX \"urllib3\\.util\\.Retry\\.DEFAULT\\_RETRY\\_AFTER\\_MAX\")\\. Any Retry-After headers larger than this value will be limited to this value\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\nDefault methods to be used for `allowed_methods`\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\nDEFAULT\\_RETRY\\_AFTER\\_MAX: [Final](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Final \"\\(in Python v3\\.14\\)\")\\[[int](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#int \"\\(in Python v3\\.14\\)\")\\] = 21600\n\nDefault maximum allowed value for Retry-After headers in seconds\n\nRETRY\\_AFTER\\_STATUS\\_CODES = frozenset\\(\\{413, 429, 503\\}\\)\n\n\n[Sourc