urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html#urllib3.util.Url \"urllib3\\.util\\.url\\.Url\")\n\nData structure for representing an HTTP URL\\. Used as a return value for [parse\\_url\\(\\)](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html#urllib3.util.parse_url \"urllib3\\.util\\.parse\\_url\")\\. Both the scheme and host are normalized as they are both case-insensitive according to RFC 3986\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n```\nimport urllib3\n\nU = urllib3.util.parse_url(\"https://google.com/mail/\")\n\nprint(U.url)\n# \"https://google.com/mail/\"\n\nprint( urllib3.util.Url(\"https\", \"username:password\",\n                        \"host.com\", 80, \"/path\", \"query\", \"fragment\"\n                        ).url\n    )\n# \"https://username:password@host.com:80/path?query#fragment\"\n\n```\n\nurllib3\\.util\\.assert\\_fingerprint\\(*cert*, *fingerprint*\\)\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\nurllib3\\.util\\.create\\_urllib3\\_context\\(*ssl\\_version=None*, *cert\\_reqs=None*, *options=None*, *ciphers=None*, *ssl\\_minimum\\_version=None*, *ssl\\_maximum\\_version=None*, *verify\\_flags=None*\\)\n\nCreates and configures an [ssl\\.SSLContext](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html#urllib3.util.SSLContext \"ssl\\.SSLContext\") instance for use with urllib3\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n[SSLContext](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html#urllib3.util.SSLContext \"urllib3\\.util\\.SSLContext\")\n\nurllib3\\.util\\.is\\_connection\\_dropped\\(*conn*\\)\n\nReturns True if the connection is dropped and should be closed\\. :param conn: [urllib3\\.connection\\.HTTPConnection](https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.connection.html#urllib3.connection.HTTPConnection \"urllib3\\.connection\\.HTTPConnection\") object\\.\n\n\n[Source passage omitted]\n\n```\nimport urllib3\n\nprint(urllib3.util.make_headers(keep_alive=True, user_agent=\"Batman/1.0\"))\n#